      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ui): make session history accessible in picker and sidebar",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes #95601 for the current Control UI session-history surface.\n\nUnlabeled chat sessions can otherwise appear as raw scoped session keys, and sidebar recent sessions did not expose enough list semantics / active-state context for assistive technologies. The current branch narrows the PR back to the live 9-file scope after rebasing on the latest `main`: readable derived session titles, sidebar list semantics, and proof that readable titles survive normal session patch refreshes.\n\n## Summary\n\n- Adds optional `derivedTitle` typing/display support for Control UI session rows.\n- For chat session history loads, forwards `includeDerivedTitles` through the sessions capability and requests it from the chat session list.\n- Uses `derivedTitle` as the readable fallback before raw session keys in session display helpers.\n- Gives sidebar recent sessions list/listitem semantics and richer accessible names that include readable title, timestamp metadata, active-state text, active-run state, and unread state.\n- Marks the active sidebar session link with `aria-current=\"page\"`.\n- Preserves the most recent `sessions.list` options when refreshing after `sessions.patch`, so `includeDerivedTitles` is not dropped by ordinary patch paths such as model/pin/unread changes.\n- Adds unit/jsdom/browser coverage for derived-title display and patch-refresh preservation.\n\n## Scope / Overlap Note\n\nThis PR is now the narrower derived-title + sidebar-accessibility slice. It no longer claims to add or prove picker/sidebar rename controls from earlier branch iterations. Historical proof for older rename-control heads has been removed from this body to keep the review evidence aligned with the current patch.\n\n## Compatibility / Migration\n\nNo migration is required.\n\n- `derivedTitle` is optional on `GatewaySessionRow` and optional in the local session-display row shape.\n- Existing serialized/cached rows without `derivedTitle` continue to fall back through the existing display order.\n- The patch-refresh change only reuses the last successful list options; it does not alter persisted session data or the `sessions.patch` RPC payload.\n\n## Evidence\n\nCurrent head: `1c622966712ebae1c3e841ca5ddfed3d7d2f0282`  \nBase checked against latest `main`: `7c0a7c8be210c7d95b0b4e6b4cf0126e5c2e7e44`\n\nPatch-quality evidence added in this head:\n\n- `ui/src/lib/sessions/index.test.ts`\n  - verifies `sessions.patch` refreshes reuse the prior list options\n  - specifically asserts `includeDerivedTitles: true` survives the post-patch `sessions.list`\n  - confirms the patch RPC payload stays unchanged (`key`, `agentId`, patch fields only)\n- `ui/src/e2e/chat-flow.e2e.test.ts`\n  - browser/DOM test sets up two `sessions.list` responses: one with `derivedTitle` only when `includeDerivedTitles` is requested, and one without it\n  - opens the Control UI chat page\n  - verifies the sidebar displays the readable derived title instead of the raw session key\n  - verifies the active sidebar link exposes `aria-current=\"page\"`\n  - performs a real UI model-change action that sends `sessions.patch`\n  - verifies the following refresh requests `includeDerivedTitles: true`\n  - verifies the sidebar still displays the readable title and keeps active accessible state after the patch refresh\n- `ui/src/pages/overview/view.render.test.ts`\n  - verifies overview recent-session rendering uses derived titles for unlabeled rows\n- `ui/src/pages/chat/chat-send.test.ts`\n  - verifies chat session list requests include derived titles\n- `git diff --check`: passed locally before push\n- Conflict scan: no unmerged files and no conflict markers before push\n\n## Current-Head GitHub Actions Evidence\n\nExact-head checks were triggered after pushing `1c622966712ebae1c3e841ca5ddfed3d7d2f0282`.\n\n- CI run: <https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28865767397>\n- Real behavior proof check: <https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28865765327>\n\nThe CI run is expected to exercise the newly added browser/DOM E2E coverage for the patch-refresh derived-title path. Once the run completes, the check output for the changed UI targets is the current-head proof that normal UI patch actions do not drop readable session titles.\n\n## Not Tested\n\n- Live macOS VoiceOver speech transcript was not re-captured for this narrower current-head patch. The browser/DOM coverage verifies the accessible names and active state that screen readers consume.\n",
        "branch": "fix/voiceover-session-history",
